# Phase-1 CCC harness backlog wires

Patterns from CCC `.local/adopts/` that agents must follow. Clones stay REFERENCE unless `wire_status: runtime_wired`.

## Schema-bound tools (nuance-mcp / K198)

- Before side-effecting MCP/tool calls: args must pass **schema / typed bounds** (reject physically or contract-impossible values).
- Prefer skills as **compositions of typed tools**, not free-form shell soup.
- Do **not** add nuance-mcp (instruments domain) to prod MCP allowlist without an operator ticket.

## Policy-as-code on artifacts (satellite-mission-compiler / K181)

- High-blast plans (deploys, LIVE Discord, trading egress, destructive git): validate **schema then policy** before execute.
- Steal layered OPA/Rego-style gates; do **not** run satellite runtime or Argo fleets from `.local/adopts/satellite-mission-compiler`.

## Validate DAG before run (DynAMO / DataFlow)

- Multi-step agent workflows: ensure a **validated DAG / ready-set** before parallel fan-out; prune context per node.
- OpenDCAI DataFlow / DynAMO clones = pattern study only — **not** TipDrop/prod deps (WebUI NOASSERTION).

## Compaction ≠ replace memory owner (LightMem2)

- Prefer **ingestion-aware compaction** and lifecycle eviction over dumping raw history.
- Do **not** replace claude-mem / wiki dual-memory with LightMem2. Clone = TokenPilot study only.

## Posterior ≠ Phase-0 (Bayesian-Agent)

- Skill/registry posteriors may rank rewrite priority — they **never** replace `@concepts/skill-vetting.md` Phase-0 (license/security).
- `.local/adopts/Bayesian-Agent` = CONDITIONAL laptop trial only.

## Skill packaging, no catalog mirror (jezweb / agents4geos / Awesome-AE)

- Steal **SKILL.md structure**, frontmatter, test hooks — file into wiki/skills.
- **No** remote catalog mirroring (LESSONS 2026-05-13). Awesome-Agent-Engineering = digest pointer only.
- agents4geos = MCP+skills packaging REFERENCE; **NO-GO** full GEOS stack (>500MB).

## ToM explanations (tars)

- When the operator is confused or asks “why”: prefer **personalized / theory-of-mind** style explanation over opaque tool dumps.
- TARS VSIX = REFERENCE — not a default Cursor extension.

## Diagrams (flowforge-skill)

- Prefer **Cursor canvas** for analytical diagrams in this federation.
- Optional NL→draw.io skill only after skill-scanner + operator OK — not required for CCC.

## Browser harness verify (fara)

- Steal **verifier-triple / synthetic env** discipline for browser checks.
- Do **not** adopt native CUA inference stacks; keep cursor-ide-browser + Webwright.

## Traceable scholarship (AIH-Infra / K210)

- Citation-first: claim + locator (`@path` / URL / DOI / quote). Unsupported → **NO_EVIDENCE**.
- AIH-Infra clone = white-paper REFERENCE — wiki citation discipline already wins.

